 reminder of the need for greater transparency and accountability in the military's use of force, and the importance of upholding human rights in the country.\n\n**Key Statistics:**\n\n* 10 people killed in the clash between soldiers and suspected oil thieves in Palmarito\n* 4 soldiers and 6 suspected criminals died in the incident\n* Mexico has the second-highest number of murders last year among countries considered in \"armed conflicts\"\n* The military has been implicated in extrajudicial killings in the past, including the killing of 22 suspects at a warehouse in Tlatlaya in 2014\n* Three",
